# L §5.18 check: "Sides read at different law dates list each"; L §8.2 the `law date <d>, cut <K>` entry: "a check
# whose sides are read at different law dates lists each".  rate is 0.1 under 2025's law and 0.12 under 2026's; the
# left side pins law 2025-06-30 (L §4.3 Pins), the right side is read at the ask's law 2026-06-30.  Difference
# 0.1 - 0.12 = -0.02.  Layout of the two dates: this interpreter's.
=== m.tally
model c
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "ustawa"
input rate: num

version v2025
  cite s
  governs 2025
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.1

version v2026
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 0.12

ask q: check rate as if {law 2025-06-30} == rate law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q: differs: rate as if {...} = 0.1, rate = 0.12, difference -0.02
...
  law date 2025-06-30 (left), 2026-06-30 (right), cut 2026-10-20
